    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/nfdi4cat/goldbook-skos/blame/main/vocabularies/goldbook/IDs00xxx/00360.ttl> ;
    skos:definition "Ion exchanger with anions as counter-ions. The term anion-exchange resin may be used in the case of solid organic polymers. The base form of an anion exchanger is the ionic form in which the counter-ions are hydroxide groups ($\\ce{OH–}$ form) or the ionogenic groups form an uncharged base, e.g. $\\ce{-NH2}$."@en ;
    skos:inScheme goldbook: ;
    skos:prefLabel "anion exchanger"@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf goldbook: ;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.A00360> ;
.
